{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And YHWH was wrathful with me for your sakes.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): He became filled with wrath against me because of your complaints; and so he mentions further on, ״ה' התאנף בי על דבריכם״ — 'HaShem was angry with me on your account'; and thus it is written (Psalms 106:32): ״וירע למשה בעבורם״." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> ״ויתעבר ה' בי״ — this is what is written (Exodus 34:6): ״ויעבור ה' על פניו״ — that is to say, at that hour when He gave me greatness for your sakes and caused His glory to pass before my face at Sinai, I entreated Him concerning this, but He did not heed me." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah:</b> ״ויתעבר ה' בי״ alludes to the mystery of the עבור (passing-through/transmigration); and this is the force of ״בי״ (in me), for it should have said ״עמי״ (with me), in the manner of what is written (Psalms 89:39): ״התעברת עם משיחך״. And it is known that the expression 'the mystery of the עבור' is from the language of עברה (wrath/transgression), for the mystery of גלגול (transmigration) in the matter of formation is governed by the attribute of דין (judgment), and this is the mystery of (Exodus 7 [20:5]) ״פוקד עון אבות״, and I have already alluded to it there. And this is what the Rabbis of blessed memory said in Berakhot: even at the hour when you are filled with wrath against them, let it be as with a pregnant woman — her needs should be before you. And some of the sages read כאשה עוברה with a כ (as a pregnant woman), and in many books it is found thus; and the reason is that they did not understand the inner meaning of the matter and took from it only its outward aspect, but the correct reading is with a ב (באשה עוברה), and so is the tradition of the sage Rabbi Isaac son of the Rabbi of blessed memory: באשה עוברה with a ב. And the reason it is called 'the mystery of the עבור' is on account of the power of the generations (כח הדורות), for He calls the generations from the beginning — that is, it is impregnated (מעובר) from the inner power; and since everything that transmigrates transmigrates through the power of the generations, therefore 'the mystery of the עבור' is called 'the power of the generations'; and moreover, the expression עבור is from the root of רבוע (squared/fourfold), because the matter involves quadrilaterals together with that which transmigrates and otherwise, sometimes three; and further, the expression עבור — because it does not pass out of (אינו עובר) its family line." "<b>It is enough for you; you shall not add.</b> The Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: ״רב לך״ — it is enough for you, what is hidden away for you, from what is written (Psalms 31:20): ״מה רב טובך אשר צפנת ליראיך״." "<b>And in the Midrash of Tanchuma:</b> ״רב לך אל תוסף״ — once the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him, ״רב לך אל תוסף״, Moses said to Him: Master of the universe! My mother Yocheved — her teeth were set on edge (נקהו שיניה) on account of her two sons; will her teeth be set on edge yet again (יקהו) on account of my death? He said to him: Thus it arose in מחשבה (thought), and such is the way of the world. End. And the meaning of מחשבה is the supernal מחשבה (thought) from which all were emanated and in which all are included; and this is the expression מחשבה, and the discerning one will understand."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:17.014026506Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}